1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,219
This is Yudhix, truth-first social intelligence.

2
00:00:03,219 --> 00:00:08,657
When a creator says something wrong about your product, thousands of angry comments follow.

3
00:00:08,657 --> 00:00:14,036
Yudhix finds which claims are false, which reactions they caused, and what to do about it.

4
00:00:15,016 --> 00:00:16,406
It works in five steps.

5
00:00:16,406 --> 00:00:17,372
Analyze a video.

6
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:20,694
Fact-check every claim against your own knowledge base.

7
00:00:20,694 --> 00:00:22,265
Read the comments with AI.

8
00:00:22,265 --> 00:00:25,104
Link each reaction to the claim that caused it.

9
00:00:25,104 --> 00:00:27,157
And reply with the official facts.

10
00:00:28,116 --> 00:00:29,464
Everything starts here.

11
00:00:29,464 --> 00:00:37,784
Paste a YouTube link, and Yudhix pulls the transcript, the video details and a sample of comments, then runs the full check in the background.

12
00:00:38,749 --> 00:00:45,874
Every analyzed video lands in this library, with its factual accuracy, disputed claims and comment volume at a glance.

13
00:00:46,849 --> 00:00:49,042
Open a video to see its truth report.

14
00:00:49,042 --> 00:00:51,768
Each claim is time-stamped and gets a verdict:

15
00:00:51,768 --> 00:00:54,316
accurate, misleading, false, or unverified.

16
00:00:54,316 --> 00:01:02,376
The verdict quotes the exact sentence from your official source, and anything the AI isn't sure about is flagged for a person to review.

17
00:01:03,328 --> 00:01:07,293
The audience impact tab shows what the comments mean for the product:

18
00:01:07,293 --> 00:01:17,351
sentiment by comments and by reach, how much of the anger comes from misinformation versus real product concerns, which topics people talk about, and how it changes over time.

19
00:01:20,094 --> 00:01:22,792
The product growth tab shows the positive side:

20
00:01:22,792 --> 00:01:29,394
what people love, who is ready to buy, and the feature requests hidden in the comments, grouped into product ideas.

21
00:01:31,227 --> 00:01:33,370
The inbox ranks comments by impact.

22
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:40,716
Each one shows whether it reacts to misinformation or to a real product issue, so the team replies with the right facts.

23
00:01:40,716 --> 00:01:44,206
Replies can be drafted by AI, citing the official source.

24
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:50,625
Every reply goes through an approval step before it is posted, with an audit trail of who approved what.

25
00:01:52,494 --> 00:01:56,184
Feature requests from all videos come together on the ideas page.

26
00:01:56,184 --> 00:02:03,339
The product team moves each idea from new, to reviewing, planned and shipped, with the original comments attached as evidence.

27
00:02:04,294 --> 00:02:07,003
The knowledge base holds your official facts.

28
00:02:07,003 --> 00:02:12,061
Upload a PDF, Word or text document, and Yudhix splits it into clauses it can quote.

29
00:02:12,061 --> 00:02:19,167
Your documents stay in your own database, and sync with your AI connection, including anything added while AI was off.

30
00:02:20,127 --> 00:02:22,441
Each workspace chooses where AI runs:

31
00:02:22,441 --> 00:02:28,946
locally on your own server, or with a cloud provider like Claude, ChatGPT or Gemini, using your own key.

32
00:02:28,946 --> 00:02:36,889
The key is checked before anything switches over, and if a provider fails, Yudhix falls back to the local model, then to rules.

33
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,546
And new comments keep coming.

34
00:02:39,546 --> 00:02:47,864
Yudhix checks every analyzed video on a schedule, reads only the new comments, and notifies the team when negativity rises or new ideas appear.

35
00:02:50,193 --> 00:02:50,619
Yudhix.

36
00:02:50,619 --> 00:02:56,167
Know which claims hurt your product, answer with facts, and learn what your customers want.

37
00:02:56,167 --> 00:02:57,569
Thank you for watching.
